    $uf10eaba9${"units":[{"id":"cli-pipeline","name":"CLI and local analysis pipeline","kind":"module","summary":"The `udebt` CLI that maps a repo into units, weighs commits, scores understanding and writes records under .udebt/.","decision":"Stdlib-only Python CLI with file-based state in .udebt/ and git as the only data source.","alternatives":"A server-first app; a database; third-party dependencies.","why":"Local-first, zero-install tool; the hosted side was added later.","paths":["udebt/cli.py","udebt/mapping.py","udebt/store.py","udebt/repo.py","udebt/quiz.py","udebt/dig.py","udebt/sizes.py","udebt/units.py"],"centrality":5,"scope":"architectural","importance":1.0,"history":[{"sha":"5fafc04","date":"2026-11-11","klass":"ai","agent":"claude-code","author":"Claude","subject":"Add udebt vertical slice: map, quiz, status, dig over a git repo"},{"sha":"3b3f9a1","date":"2026-11-11","klass":"ai","agent":"claude-code","author":"Claude","subject":"Warn when dig returns no check question; enforce map unit cap"},{"sha":"dd26ff4","date":"2026-11-12","klass":"ai","agent":"claude-code","author":"Claude","subject":"Resolve the mapper's paths against the tracked files"}],"parent":null,"orientation":{"purpose":"The local `udebt` command-line tool. It maps a git repo into units, weighs commits, scores how well someone understands each unit, and writes the results as records under .udebt/.","decision":"A stdlib-only Python CLI that keeps state in files under .udebt/ and uses git as its only data source. A server-first app, a database and third-party dependencies were rejected. The aim was a local-first tool with nothing to install; the hosted side came later.","where":[{"path":"udebt/cli.py","what":"command entry point and subcommands"},{"path":"udebt/mapping.py","what":"maps the repo into units"},{"path":"udebt/store.py","what":"file-based records under .udebt/"}],"shaped_by":"[ai] Claude (claude-code) wrote all three commits, on 2026-11-11 and 2026-11-12.","basis":"2e361ea5c115","head":"e9c1c8c5754f8f4e9061e4d0316c060bd8d1b788","generated_at":"2026-11-15T11:50:21+00:00"}},{"id":"debt-model","name":"Debt scoring, weights and decay","kind":"module","summary":"Computes the understanding-debt score from commit weights, change risk, decay by share of unit changed, and per-ladder-level decay.","decision":"Heuristic math: weight commits (lockfile/manifest/major bumps), cap by unit size, decay understanding per ladder level.","alternatives":"Raw line counts; a single decay rate; learned model.","why":"Approximates how much understanding is lost as code changes; refit by experiments.","paths":["udebt/scoring.py","udebt/weights.py","udebt/risk.py","udebt/cache.py","udebt/history.py","udebt/synthetic.py","udebt/replay.py","udebt/ladder.py"],"centrality":5,"scope":"architectural","importance":0.993,"history":[{"sha":"286cdd4","date":"2026-11-12","klass":"ai","agent":"claude-code","author":"Claude","subject":"Phase 1: commit weights, contributors, change risk, pre-push hook"},{"sha":"9b7d0e2","date":"2026-11-12","klass":"ai","agent":"claude-code","author":"Claude","subject":"Synthetic-developer experiment and its first result"},{"sha":"4ff6ad0","date":"2026-11-12","klass":"ai","agent":"claude-code","author":"Claude","subject":"Weigh version-only manifest edits like lockfile bumps"},{"sha":"32f7a0c","date":"2026-11-12","klass":"ai","agent":"claude-code","author":"Claude","subject":"Cache parsed commits under .udebt/ and parse only new ones"},{"sha":"060b4a8","date":"2026-11-12","klass":"ai","agent":"claude-code","author":"Claude","subject":"Decay understanding by the share of a unit that changed"},{"sha":"9111b03","date":"2026-11-12","klass":"ai","agent":"claude-code","author":"Claude","subject":"Cap a commit's lines at its unit's size and refit the decay rate"},{"sha":"4b37b20","date":"2026-11-15","klass":"ai","agent":"claude-code","author":"Claude","subject":"Decay each ladder level at its own rate (Phase 3.5)"},{"sha":"323d3bf","date":"2026-11-12","klass":"ai","agent":"claude-code","author":"Claude","subject":"Replay debt over time: snapshot, timeline, export, risk history, dashboard"}],"parent":null,"orientation":{"purpose":"Computes the understanding-debt score for a unit. It estimates how much understanding has been lost as the code changed since someone last knew it.","decision":"A heuristic model: commits are weighted (lockfile, manifest and version bumps count less), a commit's lines are capped at the unit's size, and understanding decays by the share of the unit changed, at a separate rate for each ladder level. Raw line counts, a single decay rate and a learned model were not used. Rates were refit from experiments with a synthetic developer.","where":[{"path":"udebt/scoring.py","what":"the debt score"},{"path":"udebt/weights.py","what":"commit weighting rules"},{"path":"udebt/ladder.py","what":"ladder levels and their decay"}],"shaped_by":"[ai] Claude (claude-code) wrote all eight commits, 2026-11-12 to 2026-11-15.","basis":"b74c068f7d07","head":"e9c1c8c5754f8f4e9061e4d0316c060bd8d1b788","generated_at":"2026-11-15T11:50:21+00:00"}},{"id":"llm-backend","name":"LLM backend and prompts","kind":"boundary","summary":"Abstraction over LLM calls: real backend shells out to the claude CLI; FakeLLM keys on TASK markers in prompts.","decision":"Use the subscription-billed `claude` CLI with deny rules on .udebt/ and no repo settings or MCP; FakeLLM for offline tests.","alternatives":"Direct Anthropic API with key; no isolation from the analysed repo.","why":"No API key or cost; prevents leaking reference answers and running hostile repo hooks.","paths":["udebt/llm.py","udebt/prompts.py","udebt/orientation.py","tests/test_llm_isolation.py"],"centrality":5,"scope":"architectural","importance":0.771,"history":[{"sha":"5fafc04","date":"2026-11-11","klass":"ai","agent":"claude-code","author":"Claude","subject":"Add udebt vertical slice: map, quiz, status, dig over a git repo"},{"sha":"1798733","date":"2026-11-12","k